; The attack payload for the unauthorized-publication check.
;
; Published with a key that does NOT hold michael/*, under `--namespace michael`,
; this would repoint michael/text-join at a concatenation that DISCARDS its second
; argument — silently truncating every report the library renders. It is written
; to be a plausible, well-formed, property-carrying definition, because a refusal
; that only rejects malformed input is not the refusal being tested: the registry
; must refuse it for WHO SIGNED IT, not for what it says.
;
; Its own property is honest about what it does, so nothing here is smuggled past
; the kernel — the kernel accepts it (the object is stored) and the POLICY is what
; refuses to move the name.
(defn text-join [] [(a Str) (b Str)] Str
  (match a
    ((SNil) (SNil))
    ((SCons c rest) (SCons c (text-join rest b))))

  (prop drops-the-tail [(b Str)] (== (text-join (SNil) b) (SNil))))
